BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jack London and Japan: Connections Across the Pacific
DTSTART:20260906T000000
DTEND:20260906T000000
UID:5a97537920ccf2c868693ee9231f44d0@jacklondonpark.com
DESCRIPTION:SOLD OUT Join us for a rare opportunity to hear distinguished 
 scholars from Japan present their research exploring the lives and relatio
 nships that connected Jack London with Japanese immigrants in early twenti
 eth-century California. This special presentation examines the remarkable 
 stories of Yoshimatsu Nakata\, who worked alongside Jack London at Beauty 
 Ranch and aboard theSnark\, and Kanae Nagasawa\, the pioneering Japanese-b
 orn winemaker whose influence helped shape California’s wine industry. 
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park\, 2400 London Ranch Road\, Glen E
 llen\, CA 95442
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/jl-speaker-series-part-4
X-SOURCE:Jack London State Historic Park
